00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.230 align:start position:0%
holding up the three-finger salute  that's become a symbol of resistance in  myanmar  the soldier looks towards the country  he's left behind  we've chosen not to reveal his identity  he says he fled his military camp in  myanmar after weeks of being ordered  to shoot at protesters  i can no longer tolerate killing my own  people innocent people  i did not want to hurt them anymore the  main reason was i did not support the  military regime i hate the hunter  the former soldier is one of many army  and police officers from myanmar  who are taking refuge in the  northeastern indian border state of  mizoram  at least 400 people are thought to have  crossed the poorest border into the town  of champaign in the past three weeks  they're being looked after by locals  many of them came with no money some of  them were families  the needs of these refugees were  provided by the church youth  associations  the ngos a student leader helping the  new arrival says most people seeking  shelter in mizoram belong to the qin  ethnic group  and have close ties with people here the  brotherhood between the people of  myanmar  burma and mizoram starts even before  burma india got independence  and as such no single notification  restrictions or instruction could  make a wall between the brotherhood of  the myanmar and mizoram  the indian government has ordered the  four north eastern states bordering  myanmar to immediately identify and  deport  what it calls illegal migrants the  soldier who says he walked for two weeks  to reach mizoram told us  that would be a death sentence i think  they'll shoot me in the head  they'll execute me mizoram's leader  agrees  chief minister zoram tanga has told  prime minister narendra modi  india can't ignore what he called the  humanitarian crisis  unfolding in our own backyard given the  historical ties between the people of  mizoram and myanmar  it appears some have chosen to resist  the central government's orders  elizabeth puranam al jazeera new delhi
 

